          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01DHBiMRv1YjxWKXeHG9CqSD",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022: \u0022concepts/retrieval-patterns.md\u0022, \u0022content\u0022: \u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Retrieval Patterns\\ndescription: Techniques for combining and ranking results from multiple retrieval methods.\\ntimestamp: 2026-01-15T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - concept/Retrieval\\n  - concept/Ranking\\n  - pattern/Hybrid-Search\\nconfidence: medium\\nconfidence_reason: \\\u0022One authoritative source on hybrid retrieval; pattern established but needs additional corroboration.\\\u0022\\n---\\n\\n## Hybrid Retrieval\\n\\n**Hybrid retrieval** combines sparse lexical search (e.g. BM25) with dense vector search, then merges the two ranked result sets, often via reciprocal rank fusion, to capture both exact term matches and semantic similarity. \\n\\nThis approach consistently outperforms either method alone, particularly on queries that mix rare identifiers (error codes, product SKUs) with natural language intent. Hybrid retrieval has become the default retrieval pattern in production RAG systems.\\n\\n### Components\\n\\n- **Sparse lexical search** (e.g. BM25): Matches exact term occurrences; excels at finding documents containing rare identifiers.\\n- **Dense vector search**: Encodes query and documents as embeddings; captures semantic similarity beyond exact matches.\\n- **Reciprocal rank fusion**: A merge strategy that combines the two ranked lists into a single consolidated result set.\\n\\n### When to Use\\n\\nHybrid retrieval is especially effective for:\\n- Queries mixing structured identifiers with natural language (e.g. \\\u0022What does error code E404 mean in our logs?\\\u0022)\\n- Domains where both precision (exact terms) and semantic understanding (intent) matter\\n- Production RAG systems requiring robust performance across diverse query types\\n\\n## Other Patterns\\n\\nUse reciprocal rank fusion for robust retrieval.\\n\\n## Citations\\n\\n[^1]: Hybrid retrieval evaluation and production patterns (eval://update-over-duplicate/sample-10)\\n\u0022}"
